    restoration_trigger: "BOTH halves, and the row retires only when both are satisfied: (a) a cadence that actually executes offline-homed witnesses exists, so a green witness under such a path has a truthful admission row to write; AND (b) a required run enters the discovery-corpus path, so refuse_unexecuted_deferred_witnesses can fire when it does not. Half (a) is gunbc.rung_drop.shared_capability missing_cadence_category. Waiters whose remaining unsatisfied condition is only that capability retire together. Half (b) is not that capability. When (a) fires and (b) is still unsatisfied, this identity is removed from missing_cadence_category.waiter_identities in the SAME change as those retirements (delist, not SplitRetirement) and this row stays Standing until (b) fires. If (b) is already satisfied when (a) fires, retire with the enrolled set. (b) firing first does not delist: the row stays enrolled until (a)."
